      "faqs": [
        [
          "Is Notion better than Coda for note-taking?",
          "Yes — Notion originated as a note-taking tool and retains strengths for capturing and organizing information in a flexible, block-based interface. Coda can handle notes but is optimized more for structured workflows and lightweight app building."
        ],
        [
          "Does Coda have a free tier?",
          "Yes — Coda's free plan includes unlimited pages, 50 objects and basic automations. Notion's free plan allows up to 10 guests which can be limiting for growing teams."
        ],
        [
          "Which tool is better for building internal tools?",
          "Coda is specifically designed for this use case. Its combination of documents, spreadsheets and app-like features in one canvas lets teams create lightweight tools for project tracking, CRM lite or internal workflows without engineering support."
        ],
        [
          "How do the AI features compare?",
          "Notion's AI works as a contextual writing assistant throughout the interface. Coda's AI focuses on helping build structures and automations from natural language descriptions. They serve different primary purposes within their respective tools."
        ],
        [
          "Can I migrate from Notion to Coda (or vice versa)?",
          "Both tools support markdown and CSV import/export, but direct migration of complex databases or workflows requires manual rebuilding. Notion's strength in linked databases doesn't translate directly to Coda's table-based approach, and vice versa."
